{
    "background_story": "Kora, a sleek red fox, roamed the dense forest with her bushy tail held high. However, her life took a turn for the worse when she contracted a severe case of sarcoptic mange, caused by the parasitic mite Sarcoptes scabiei. The relentless itching and painful lesions made it difficult for her to hunt and care for herself. As her condition worsened, Kora became isolated, afraid to interact with her fellow foxes. But she refused to give up. With the help of a kind wildlife rehabilitator, Kora received the treatment she needed to overcome the infestation. After months of recovery, her thick fur grew back, and she regained her strength. Kora's resilience in the face of adversity earned her a new nickname among the forest dwellers: the 'Unyielding One'. She continued to thrive, always mindful of the challenges she had overcome.",
